KNOWNBUG: N5008 [temp.alias]/2 + [temp.deduct.type] + [temp.variadic]/4-5.
Deducing a parameter pack through a QUALIFIED alias template (`N::idxseq<J...>`).
The unqualified case is handled (cpp17_alias_template_nontype_pack_deduce, CORE);
here the alias-expansion branch in guess_template_args is restricted to
UNqualified template-ids (an anti-recursion guard for a libstdc++ regex
member-alias shape), so the qualified alias is never expanded and the pack is
not deduced ("found no match for symbol 'f'", CONVERSION ERROR, EXIT=6) -- so the
desired-behaviour desc above does not match and this registers as a known bug.
This is exactly how std::apply uses `std::index_sequence<_Idx...>` (a qualified
alias) and is the remaining cpp17_apply_basic blocker.  g++ runs r == 3; clang++
accepts.  Flip to CORE once a qualified alias template's pack is deduced.
